FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-gpu-blob.patch last among them. It carries command submission, fences and wait for slice GP4 (lane gp4-submit):
- virtio-gpud/src/submit.rs: asynchronous SUBMIT_3D with VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_FENCE, VIRTIO_GPU_FLAG_INFO_RING_IDX, monotonic fence ids and ring index, completed from the control queue via the existing FrameWake and poll_pending loop without busy-waiting.
- driver-graphics/src/submit.rs: DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_EXECBUFFER (bounded command size, BO handle count and syncobj count; syncobj_stride == 16 only when syncobj counts are nonzero; FENCE_FD_IN refused with EOPNOTSUPP; FENCE_FD_OUT exported via dup as a bounded FenceResource answering poll/fevent once signaled and read with 16-byte VirtgpuFenceState) and DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_WAIT (non-blocking NOWAIT or readiness-based wait on a resource's last fence, ENOENT for unknown resources).

